Z||000012||Fformula88||08-24-2000||05:46 PM||||With all great looks of the redesign, its a wonder why they didn't give it a chance.  Obviously the redesign money had already been spent because the new bodies exist.  Pontiac only had to tool up for production, and the dies for the plastics are a lot cheaper than steel cars.  They should have given the redesign a chance at saving the Fiero!  I suree would buy one!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fformula88||08-24-2000||05:53 PM||||The pics in the yard are from the US, taken by an Australian tour.  They are in the Pontiac special Vehicle compunds in Detroit Michigan.<P>On a sad not, the first page of the web page that those redesigned Fiero pics are from shows this...<P><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.pontiworld.com.au/newsletter/july2000/img3.gif">   <P>I love those blue Fieros.  What a shame.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<P>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 08-24-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 08-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||rockcrawl||08-24-2000||07:38 PM||||No kidding, the styling on that car was way ahead of it's time! It looks like something that would do very well even in today's market. I hate looking at those pictures though, it gives me very bad feelings toward GM for cancelling it.<P> So, what do you think one of those prototypes would sell for at auction?<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
